hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17738","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salama, narrated to us, from Ikrima ibn Khalid, from his father, or from his uncle, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in the expedition of Tabuk: If plague is in a land and you are in it, do not go out of it. And if it is in a land and you are not in it, do not approach it."
